      "exit_code": 0,
      "stdout": "usage: spec-dock work finish [-h] target\n\npositional arguments:\n  target\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n\nTarget:\n  The explicit Scope selector (or @current selection) in this worktree.\n\nReads:\n  Current metadata, required target and descendant lifecycle, and this worktree's captured direct record. GitHub-backed completion is confirmed completed by a live GET before clearing that record.\n\nWrites:\n  Complete the Scope, then clear the captured direct record only if it selects that Scope or a descendant; keep the current branch.\n\nDoes not:\n  Keeps the current branch; no Start lock, automatic parent selection, child completion, commit, push, merge, or rollback. A Scope outside the active chain leaves the direct record unchanged.\n\nPreconditions:\n  The explicit Scope must resolve and its completion guards must pass. A Scope outside the active chain can be completed without changing the current selection.\n\nConfirmation:\n  Apply requires --yes; --dry-run needs no confirmation.\n\nEffects:\n  Complete the Scope, then clear the captured direct record only if it selects that Scope or a descendant; keep the current branch.\n\nRecovery:\n  Inspect current completion and direct selection, then issue a new explicit Finish; no journal or rollback.\n\nJSON:\n  --json returns one specdock.cli/v2 envelope. Data: kind=work-finish, scope_id, completed, branch_before, branch_after, selection_token; effects report completion and any captured-record clear separately.\n\nExamples:\n  spec-dock work finish <scope-id>\n",
